To add the bibliography to the table of contents when using the `biblatex` package with the `bibtex` backend, you can use the `heading=bibintoc` option in the `\printbibliography` command. This option adds the bibliography to the table of contents with the title "Bibliography". Here's an example:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[backend=bibtex,urldate=iso]{biblatex}
\addbibresource{bibliography.bib}

\begin{document}

\tableofcontents

\section{Introduction}
This is an introduction.

\printbibliography[heading=bibintoc]

\end{document}
```

In this example, the `\printbibliography[heading=bibintoc]` command adds the bibliography to the table of contents. The `bibliography.bib` file contains the bibliography entries.

Note that the `heading=bibintoc` option is not available when using the `biber` backend. If you are using the `biber` backend, you can use the `heading=bibnumbered` option instead. This option adds the bibliography to the table of contents with the title "Bibliography" and a section number. Here's an example:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage[backend=biber,urldate=iso]{biblatex}
\addbibresource{bibliography.bib}

\begin{document}

\tableofcontents

\section{Introduction}
This is an introduction.

\printbibliography[heading=bibnumbered]

\end{document}
```

In this example, the `\printbibliography[heading=bibnumbered]` command adds the bibliography to the table of contents with the title "Bibliography" and a section number. The `bibliography.bib` file contains the bibliography entries.

